# Build output installed here by `scripts/build.mts`. Committing a 2.5 MB addon
# and two DLLs would put binaries in the repo and guarantee a stale one is
# eventually loaded; `package.json`'s `files` list is what ships them.
aethervfs.node
vfs_shim_dll.dll
vfs_payload.dll

# `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` output. The sources are `index.mts`, `native.mts`
# and `provider-host.mts`, and they sit beside their outputs — which works only
# because `.mts` and `.mjs` are different extensions, and which keeps
# `import.meta.dirname` meaning the same directory in both.
#
# **`index.d.mts` is in here on purpose.** A hand-written `index.d.ts` used to be
# committed beside a hand-written `index.cjs`; the whole point of the TypeScript
# migration's task 2 is that the declaration is emitted, and a committed copy of
# a build output is how it starts drifting again. `package.json`'s `files` list
# is what ships it.
#
# The package was CommonJS before the ESM migration's task 2, and these are the
# `.cjs`/`.d.cts` outputs from then — still ignored in case a stale one from an
# old build survives on someone's disk.
index.mjs
index.d.mts
native.mjs
native.d.mts
provider-host.mjs
provider-host.d.mts
index.cjs
index.d.cts
native.cjs
native.d.cts
provider-host.cjs
provider-host.d.cts
*.tsbuildinfo

# The stand-in executable the demo launches. Built, not authored.
#
# Anchored to this directory (`/fixtures/`, not `fixtures/`) on purpose: an
# unanchored pattern matches a directory named `fixtures` at any depth, which
# swallowed `test/fixtures/` — the ESM migration's task 4 fixture modules,
# authored, not built, and meant to be committed.
/fixtures/

# The package has npm **devDependencies** as of the TypeScript migration —
# vitest, typescript and @types/node — and no runtime dependencies, which is the
# part that was always deliberate. `pnpm-lock.yaml` is committed (it is the point
# of `--frozen-lockfile` in CI); `node_modules/` is not.
node_modules/
